<body>
  <GameNav />
  <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &gt; <a href="/rooms-and-exits/">Rooms &amp; Exits</a> &gt; Chapter 3 &gt; Level 20</nav>

  <main class="seo-section">
    <h1>Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 3 Level 20 Walkthrough: Kids Bedroom 2</h1>

    <p>Kids Bedroom 2 is room 20 of 24 in Chapter 3, <i>Murder Dressed in White</i>, and it is a second pass at the child's-bedroom idea. Where Kids Bedroom 1 was a hub of ten loose toys, this one is a tighter chain: a dark space under the bed that needs light, a battery and a flashlight that make that light, and a stained-glass tile board on a wooden chest that only gives up its drawer once the board is finished. Everything after that is pickups feeding a single ornate jewel box on the desk.</p>

    <div class="disclaimer">Unofficial fan-made guide. Not affiliated with Webelinx Games, the developer of Rooms &amp; Exits: Escape Room Games.</div>

    <div class="verify-note">Rebuilt from the full 4:20 recording at one frame per second. Item names are quoted from the game's own white captions — <b>Zipper</b> (0:13), <b>Battery</b> (0:16), <b>Flashlight</b> (0:38), <b>Turned on flashlight</b> (0:44), <b>Screwdriver</b> (2:16) — and the end card was read from two separate frames plus a 4x crop of the numbers. All three end-card reads agree on <b>+50</b> and <b>Time: 4:10</b>. Anything that only ever read one way, or that two passes read differently, is listed under "What this page could not verify".</div>

    <LevelSelector chapter={3} current={20} variant="jump" label="Chapter 3 · Murder Dressed in White" />

    <div class="answer-box">
      <span class="label">Quick answer</span>
      <p>The room runs on objects rather than typed digits. The chain is: <b>Battery</b> + <b>Flashlight</b> → light under the bed → stained-glass tile board on the chest → drawer opens → jewel box on the desk.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the pink ottoman at <b>0:05</b>, then check the cloud shelf for the <b>Zipper</b> (0:13) and the <b>Battery</b> (0:16).</li>
        <li>At <b>0:26</b> the space under the bed is black. Combine the battery with the flashlight in the inventory, then use it: <b>Turned on flashlight</b>, 0:44.</li>
        <li>Under the bed now shows a wooden chest. Its lid is the tile board: square tiles with four coloured triangular facets, stacks either side. Match colours edge to edge.</li>
        <li>The finished board opens the chest's drawer at about <b>1:49</b>. Take what is inside and keep moving: the panda teepee holds the <b>Screwdriver</b> at <b>2:16</b>.</li>
        <li>Collect the jewels and the <b>cloud softpillow</b> colour tag, then fill the <b>five sockets</b> on the jewel box at the desk from about <b>3:30</b>.</li>
        <li>The level ends at <b>4:18</b>: +50 coins, Time 4:10.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="video-wrap">
      <div class="yt-facade" data-yt="C8Fn9aoJ9Vw" data-title="Rooms &amp; Exits Level 20 Kids Bedroom 2 Walkthrough Murder Dressed in White Chapter 3"
           role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Play video: Rooms &amp; Exits Level 20 Kids Bedroom 2 Walkthrough">
