    <h2>What this page could not verify<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <div class="warn">
      Four things, stated plainly so you know which parts of this page are reads and which are reconstruction.
      <br><br>
      <b>1. The cell count of the tile board.</b> Three passes read the board as three rows of three, as three rows of four, and as four rows of four with fourteen filled and two empty; the loose-tile stacks also change size between frames as tiles are taken. The mechanic (edge matching, four triangular facets per tile) and the completion (last tile at about 1:49, drawer opens) are both solid; the exact grid is not, so no count is printed.
      <br><br>
      <b>2. The middle colour of the softpillow cloud.</b> Two crops agree on the order green, red, then purple, yellow at the end, and on the letter mapping (c green, l red, u purple, d yellow). They disagree on the third segment, which read once as blue and once as cyan. The order above uses blue; swap it for cyan if the socket will not take a blue gem.
      <br><br>
      <b>3. What the chest drawer contained.</b> The drawer clearly slides out after the board is finished, and the frame we checked shows a bare wooden interior. An earlier pass thought it saw a small pale object inside, so we describe the drawer and the timing and do not name contents.
      <br><br>
      <b>4. The purpose of the Zipper and the Screwdriver.</b> Both are real pickups with real captions, and neither is visibly used before the level ends. They may belong to the jewel-box sequence in a way the camera skips, or to a later room. We are not going to invent a use for them.
    </div>
